    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2025/11/puma-velocity-nitro-4-review-2025.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: Full-length NITROFOAM provides moderate cushioning with a softer heel transition and firmer forefoot push-off, and the forefoot feels more protective than its stack suggests.",
        "Responsiveness: The ride offers moderate bounce and a snappy toe-off, but the flexible forefoot and low rocker make it feel more natural than highly propulsive.",
        "Stability: Forefoot flexibility suggests limited torsional rigidity; a snug midfoot/rearfoot and semi-rigid to moderately stiff heel counter improve hold, but the clunky, medially biased heel with lateral flare can feel unstable.",
        "Durability: The full-length PUMAGRIP outsole has excellent wet-road grip and showed no visible wear after ~25 miles, with above-average longevity expected."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Road Trail Run",
      "priority": 4,
      "url": "https://www.roadtrailrun.com/2025/07/puma-velocity-nitro-4-review-5.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The all-NitroFoam midsole is soft and protective with good heel cushioning, but forefoot cushioning is noticeably thinner (10 mm drop) with more ground feel and some midfoot mushiness.",
        "Responsiveness: The ride is lively and bouncy with strong energy return/pop and works for uptempo efforts, though the soft midfoot can slightly blunt transition snappiness.",
        "Stability: A rigid high heel counter and secure lockdown help rearfoot control, but overall stability/torsional support is lower than prior versions due to the softer platform and less forefoot/midfoot structure.",
        "Durability: The upper/overlays are reported durable with no visible wear after about 60 miles, outsole grip/rubber coverage is strong, but minimal toe reinforcement and a softer outsole that picks up debris are potential longevity concerns."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Believe in the Run",
      "priority": 5,
      "url": "https://believeintherun.com/shoe-reviews/puma-velocity-nitro-4-review/",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The full-length NitroFoam and 36/26 mm stack provide comfortable impact protection with a balanced, not-soft feel, with more heel presence than forefoot from the 10 mm drop.",
        "Responsiveness: The ride is described as responsive with solid bounce and a light, snappy feel that can handle both daily miles and uptempo intervals.",
        "Stability: A narrow, suction-like midfoot wrap and secure fit give reliable lateral hold for narrow feet, though explicit torsional rigidity and heel-counter stiffness details are not provided.",
        "Durability: The generous PUMAGRIP outsole is highlighted as tacky, flexible, and durable, with excellent grip and strong outsole longevity expectations."
      ]
    }
  ],
